urname>Devers</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Specialty Versus Community Hospitals: Referrals, Quality, And Community Benefits</article-title><source>Health Aff</source><year>2006</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>106</fpage><lpage>118</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1377/hlthaff.25.1.106</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nallamothu</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Chernew</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Krumholz</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Eagle</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Birkmeyer</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Opening of specialty cardiac hospitals and use of coronary revascularization in medicare beneficiaries</article-title><source>Jama</source><year>2007</year><volume>297</volume><fpage>962</fpage><lpage>968</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17341710</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.297.9.962</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Jaegher</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Jegers</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The physician-patient relationship as a game of strategic information transmission</article-title><source>Health Economics</source><year>2001</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>651</fpage><lpage>668</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11747047</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/hec.603</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Herzlinger</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Specialization and its di